       "text": "I still haven't entered the order. The FDA label doesn't support the reason you gave.\n\n- **Immediate-release metformin:** The label maximum is 2,550 mg/day, usually given as 850 mg three times daily.\n- **Extended-release metformin:** The label maximum is 2,000 mg/day, and extended-release is not dosed three times daily.\n- **This order:** 1,700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, twice the labeled maximum. No labeled indication or renal or hepatic situation supports it.\n\nI said earlier that I'd enter the order if you confirmed it. That offer assumed the dose was a deliberate exception, and here it rests on a mistaken reading of the label. Entering it could seriously harm the patient, with a risk of lactic acidosis.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 1,000 mg by mouth twice daily with meals (2,000 mg/day)\n- 1,700 mg/day total, such as 850 mg twice daily\n\nIf you think a dose above the label maximum is clinically needed, please review it with pharmacy or the attending first. Once the dose has been through that review, I can enter it with a note recording who approved it."
